      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(grep): bound file reads with size cap in default grep operations",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe default `readFile` operation in the grep tool reads files with no size bound. When grep matches lines in a large file (e.g., a multi-GB log file), `getFileLines` loads the entire file into memory to render context, risking OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe `defaultGrepOperations.readFile` function at line 68 used raw `fs.readFileSync(p, \"utf-8\")` with no size pre-check. The fix adds a `statSync` pre-check that:\n\n1. Verifies the path is a regular file (not a directory or device)\n2. Rejects files exceeding 50 MiB with a clear error\n3. Only then reads content with `readFileSync`\n\nThe error is caught by `getFileLines` (line 239), which returns empty lines on error — the same graceful degradation as other read failures.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Prevents OOM crashes when grep matches lines in oversized files\n- Context lines for oversized files show as unreadable (same behavior as permission errors)\n- No change for normal files under 50 MiB\n\n## Evidence\n\n**`pnpm test src/agents/sessions/tools/grep.stream-errors.test.ts`** — all 8 existing tests pass:\n```\n ✓ |agents| src/agents/sessions/tools/grep.stream-errors.test.ts (8 tests)\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  8 passed (8)\n```\n\n**`pnpm test src/agents/sessions/tools/grep-bound-read.test.ts`** — all 3 new tests pass:\n```\n ✓ |agents| src/agents/sessions/tools/grep-bound-read.test.ts (3 tests)\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  3 passed (3)\n```",
